    context: "Paul wrote Ephesians to believers who needed to know their place in God's plan. In a world of social rank, he told them they were chosen before the foundation of the world. David praised God for his intricate making of the human person. Today, young people face pressure to define themselves by grades, looks, followers, wealth, sport, tribe or romantic status. When these fail or change, identity collapses. The gospel offers a stable foundation.",
