    context: "Paul said that salvation is by grace, not works, and then immediately said that we are saved for good works. God also gave Bezalel and Oholiab special skills to build the tabernacle, showing that crafts and arts are gifts too. In Romans and Corinthians, Paul listed gifts like teaching, giving, leading, mercy and administration, and stressed they are for the common good. Young people often compare their gifts with others or wait for a dramatic revelation.",
