    intro: "And the Lord came and stood, calling as at other times, Samuel! Samuel! And Samuel said, Speak, for your servant hears. And Samuel grew, and the Lord was with him and let none of his words fall to the ground. And all Israel knew that Samuel was established as a prophet of the Lord.",
    context: "In Samuel's day the word of the Lord was rare and visions were not widespread. Samuel served in the temple as a boy, sleeping near the ark. Eli, the priest, was old, and his sons were corrupt. God's word to Samuel was a judgement on Eli's house. Samuel was afraid to tell Eli, but Eli insisted, and Samuel told him everything. As Samuel grew, the Lord was with him and all Israel recognised him as a prophet.",
